# "If you win the flip, gain control of that spell and you may choose new targets for it." Bot2's Lightning Bolt aims at
# Bot1; the flip is won (the first face of the coin), Bot1 takes the Bolt and aims it at Bot2, who goes to 17. The Bolt
# is still Bot2's card, so it ends in Bot2's graveyard. Its mirror, a lost flip, is the scenario for the countered Bolt.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Island
Invert Polarity
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x3
Mountain x12

[Dice]
1

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Invert Polarity.Cast(Lightning Bolt)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Invert Polarity
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
